    {
      "area": "series and episode identity",
      "result": "PASS",
      "observation": "Light screenshots at 1440×1000 and 390×844 show Redis identity, EP.52 and lesson 6/6, wrapped episode title, chapter navigation and article text fitting their viewport. Six-slug series membership is supported by the existing DOM report; the screenshots themselves show only the visible portion of the catalog."
    },
    {
      "area": "visible style and mechanism",
      "result": "PASS",
      "observation": "Cold silver backgrounds, Redis red emphasis and dark text remain distinct. The actual decoded first frame contrasts A90/C70; Figure 0 shows sampled C70/D60/E50 and candidate copies sorted E→D→C; Figure 1 shows I replacing C and retained D60 beating new F40/G30/H20. The last body frame states the approximate-ranking limit. No visible clipping was found in these decoded frames."
    },
    {
      "area": "reference boundary and fullscreen",
      "result": "PASS_WITH_VIEWPORT_LIMITS",
      "observation": "Actual decoded frames 4313, 4388 and 4462 show only the reference title and Key eviction/evict.c credited to Redis, with no burned body caption. Desktop and actual 844×390 Fullscreen API reference screenshots retain native controls without covering those titles/credits. At 390 portrait, embedded and fullscreen reference text fits but is physically small; this does not establish comfortable detailed reading on a phone."
    },
    {
      "area": "paused native player controls",
      "result": "RECORDED_LIMITATION",
      "observation": "Initial desktop/mobile poster screenshots contain a native white loading arc at player center. Embedded paused Figure playback screenshots retain the native gradient/timebar over the lower burned caption; the actual 844×390 paused fullscreen body screenshot also darkens and partly obscures its lower caption. Main keys and candidate-pool labels remain visible. Desktop fullscreen has enough letterboxing to keep the mechanism and caption clear. These captures must not be described as idle posters or universally unobscured mobile paused captions."
    },
    {
      "area": "quote popovers and citations",
      "result": "PASS_WITH_SCROLL_LIMITS",
      "observation": "R1/R2/A1/A2 popovers fit the desktop and 390-wide captured viewports; English/code excerpts wrap and Chinese explanations remain readable. Source titles/URLs agree with the existing browser report. Long panels require internal scrolling; not all metadata is visible at once. In the captured mobile A1 scroll position the header/close control is not visible; do not infer a permanently visible close control. Enter/Escape and R1 citation-after-scroll are existing browser checks, not interactions rerun in this review."
    },
    {
      "area": "article Figures and original image",
      "result": "PASS_WITH_VIEWPORT_LIMITS",
      "observation": "The exact decoded Figure frames match the stated pool and retained-candidate meanings, and the player captures after Figure replay show the D60 scene. Original-image screenshots show the actual pool JPG opened in the browser image viewer at desktop and 390 widths. Mobile fit-to-width is small; zoom/pinch and full article Figure-card controls were not separately captured. Figure decode/replay at 67.5s and 95.7333s are supported by the existing browser report."
    },
    {
